Article 14
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 11 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.
(2) The forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
a. establishing family partners at the kelurahan level;
b. establishing child and women protection units within community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of children's rights and women's rights;
d. providing first aid to victims; and
e. reporting to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.
(4) The forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 13
(1) The Regional Government implements efforts to protect children and women victims of violence through:
a. implementing protection policies for children and women victims of violence applied by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of children and women victims of violence;
c. formation of PPT;
d. guaranteeing the implementation of ease of services for victims;
e. pursuing effectiveness and efficiency for the victim recovery process; and
f. pursuing the creation of cooperation and coordination in victim recovery efforts.
(2) In order to implement the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, the regional government establishes action programs and activities for the protection of children and women in 1 (one) Regional Action Plan as the basis for regional apparatus in implementing protection for women and children victims of violence.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).
(4) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be further regulated by a Regent's Regulation.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence, is carried out based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. justice;
c. non-discrimination; and
d. victim protection;

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF KONAWE,

Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that children and women are vulnerable groups experiencing violence where all forms of violence against children and women constitute violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity thus requiring legal protection to protect their self-respect and dignity and to guarantee their right to life in accordance with their natural disposition and inherent nature without discrimination;
c. that violence against children and women in Konawe Regency shows quite high numbers and continues to increase, thus requiring protection efforts;
d. that all forms of violence against children and women constitute violations of human rights thus their dignity needs to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature without discrimination;
e. that the implementation of Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence in Konawe Regency needs to be supported by institutions and regulations so as to guarantee its implementation;
f. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, letter d and letter e above, it is deemed necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence in Konawe Regency;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);
